## How development works in this project

This project uses the [claude-dev-team](https://gitlab.your-internal-host/your-namespace/claude-dev-team) skill bundle. The conventions:

- **Vertical slices only.** Every issue cuts through the full stack end-to-end. One slice = one focused work session, one user-visible behavior change.
- **Phase commands** drive the workflow. Start a slice with `/work-start`, finish design with `/work-design-done`, push and review with `/work-review`, close out with `/work-done`.
- **Docs are per-slice, not batched.** Every slice that changes user-visible behavior updates `docs/user-guide/`. Every slice that introduces a new failure mode updates `docs/troubleshooting/`. Every slice that changes IT-Ops-relevant setup or troubleshooting updates `docs/ops/` (which auto-publishes to Notion on merge to main).
- **ADRs for non-obvious design choices.** Use `/grill-with-docs` when a decision deserves recording.

